#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid-PIC absorbing-field-wall test: a transverse shear-Alfven wave (HybridWave
testcase) lives in a finite-x domain whose x faces are ABSORBING (outgoing
characteristic) field boundaries and REFLECTING particle boundaries.  Validates
that the absorbing field BC is wired into the hybrid cell-centred advance and
that the run stays finite/stable (no NaN).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
32                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
absorb                  fieldBoxBoundaryLo
absorb                  fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

Reflecting particle walls keep the ions (and hence the hybrid Ohm's-law moments)
inside the cavity.
#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

Ideal frozen-in Ohm's law (Hall OFF) so the wave is a driven by the motional
field alone.
#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is the implicit massless
neutralizing fluid.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho
0.0                     ux
0.0                     uy
0.0                     uz
10000.0                 T
1.0439e-8               bx
0.0                     by
0.0                     bz
0.0                     ex
0.0                     ey
0.0                     ez

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI
1.0e5                   uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    npcelx
1                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii pic       plotString
100                     dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx
rhoS0 uxS0 uyS0 uzS0 Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez   plotVar

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
13.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
